const e={"seo.purpose":"Who the blur faces before posting helps","seo.purpose.p1":"Before posting to social media or a group chat, box the strangers' faces, licence plates, addresses or order numbers in your photo and pixelate or blur them.","seo.purpose.p2":"Handy for dashcam stills, street shots, unboxing photos showing shipping labels, or group photos where other kids' faces should be hidden.","seo.why":"Why use our blur faces before posting","seo.why.p1":"Photos are processed only in your browser and never uploaded, so the original never sits on someone else's server.","seo.why.li1":"Drag to draw boxes yourself; add as many as you need","seo.why.li2":"Choose pixelate or blur and adjust the strength","seo.why.li3":"Undo the last box or clear them all","seo.faq":"Blur faces before posting FAQ","seo.faq.q1":"Does it detect faces or plates automatically?","seo.faq.q1a":"No. You mark the areas to hide yourself.","seo.faq.q2":"Is my photo uploaded?","seo.faq.q2a":"No. Everything happens on your device.","seo.faq.q3":"Can the pixelation be reversed?","seo.faq.q3a":"The downloaded image has the pixels inside each box replaced, with no original data kept. A coarser setting hides more.","seo.faq.q4":"Which formats work?","seo.faq.q4a":"JPG, PNG and WebP up to 20 MB; convert HEIC first. The result downloads as PNG."};export{e as default};
